C Extension to Other Optimization Algorithms
C.1 Momentum
In this subsection we use momentum SGD as an example to show how does the discrete version of the fast equilibrium conjecture look like. Throughout this section we will assume all the momentum factors are constant, and we only care about the role of LR η and WD factor λ in the discrete dynamics.
For fixed LR η and WD λ, the formula of SGD with momentum can be written as follows:
vt+1 ← βvt + (∇L(wt; Bt) + λwt)
wt+1 ← wt − ηvt+1,
which is also equivalent to
wt+1 − wt = β(wt − wt−1) − η(∇L(wt; Bt) + λwt).
